---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro"
---

<Base title="Docs — Interscript">
  <h1 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">Documentation</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Getting started</h2>
    <p>
      Interscript is available as a Ruby gem and (in development) a TypeScript
      package. Choose your runtime:
    </p>

    <h3>Ruby</h3>
    <pre class="rounded-md bg-ink/5 p-4"><code>gem install interscript
interscript -s bgnpcgn-ukr-Cyrl-Latn-2019 input.txt</code></pre>

    <h3>TypeScript</h3>
    <pre class="rounded-md bg-ink/5 p-4"><code>npm install interscript-ts</code></pre>

    <h2>Map catalogues</h2>
    <p>
      Maps are versioned and tagged by authority. Browse the
      <a href="/maps">map explorer</a> for a sample.
    </p>

    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <p>
      See <a href="https://github.com/interscript/interscript">the monorepo</a>
      for technical design.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
